 us Notices
DESCRIPTION:This page's content changed since the last check. Visit the pa
 ge directly to review the update.\n\nWhat changed (text excerpt):\nAdded:\
 n  + October jurors selected for Panel A (State v Theriault) are to report
  for trial at 8:30AM on Tuesday\, October 27\n  + .\n  + Jurors selected f
 or Panel B (State v Dubeau) are to check this website after 4:30PM on Frid
 ay\, October 30\n  + th\n  + for reporting instructions for trial on Monda
 y\, November 2\n  + nd\n  + .\n  + All October 2026 trial jurors who have 
 NOT been selected for the cases mentioned previously are no longer expecte
 d to check this website or report for jury service. Your jury service is n
 ow completed for 5 years with the thanks of the court!\n  + All jurors sel
 ected for Panel A\, State of Maine VS. Paul Lewis\, please report to the C
 apital Judicial Center at 8:30 AM on Tuesday\, October 27\, 2026. Thank yo
 u and have a pleasant evening.\n  + Waldo County Superior Court - Belfast\
 n  + All Jurors selected for State vs Nicole Nadeau please report to the W
 aldo County Court on Friday October 30th at 9:00 am for the start of the t
 rial. Upon arrival please report to Courtroom #2 upstairs and check in wit
 h the Jury Clerk.\n  + If you have any questions\, please call 338-3107 Mo
 nday through Friday between 8 am and 4 pm.\n  + PROHIBITION OF ELECTRONIC 
 DEVICES:\n  + Please be advised that pursuant to Administrative Order JB-2
 0-01\, use of electronic devices during trial or while in deliberations ar
 e prohibited and all devices will need to be temporarily surrendered. Duri
 ng jury selection\, all devices must be turned off.\n  + October 26\, 2026
 \n  + There are no jury trials at the Yo\n[diff truncated]\nhttps://www.co
